{"seq":3,"slug":"lifecycle-and-ecology","title":"生命周期与生态人类学","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/specialized-research-areas/lifecycle-and-ecology","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"childhood-aging-lifecycle","title":"儿童、老龄化与生命周期人类学：通过仪式与照料政治","url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/specialized-research-areas/lifecycle-and-ecology/childhood-aging-lifecycle","wordCount":2639,"readingTime":11},{"seq":2,"slug":"disaster-environment-ecology","title":"灾害、环境与生态人类学：从适应到脆弱性","url":"/l-doc-books/h/anthropology/specialized-research-areas/lifecycle-and-ecology/disaster-environment-ecology","wordCount":2734,"readingTime":11}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"生命周期与生态人类学-简介\">生命周期与生态人类学 简介</h1><p>本章把人类学带回两个最基础的维度：生命历程（每个人都要经历出生、成长与衰老）与环境关系（每个社会都嵌在生态过程之中）。这两个专题的当代形态有一个共同的理论底色——<strong>拒绝自然主义</strong>：童年不是生物事实而是制度安排，「自然灾害」不是自然事件而是社会脆弱性的显影。</p>\n<p><strong>儿童、老龄化与生命周期人类学：通过仪式与照料政治</strong>从范热内普 1909 年的三段结构讲到特纳的阈限理论，再用阿里耶斯及其批评者校准「童年的发明」这一命题；年龄组制度一节展示马赛人如何把生物时间改造成跨氏族组织；老龄化部分锚定硬数据（WHO：2050 年 60+ 人口达 21 亿；日本 65+ 占比 29.1%）并分析介护保险的得失；结尾以《儿童权利公约》与玻利维亚童工法的冲突收束到政策现场。</p>\n<p><strong>灾害、环境与生态人类学：从适应到脆弱性</strong>沿理论史推进：斯图尔德的文化生态学 → 拉帕波特的能量流模型 → 布莱基与沃茨的政治生态学；核心工具是 UNDRR 风险公式 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R = H \\times E \\times V / C</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0077em;\">R</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span></span></span></span></span>，并以海地、新奥尔良、土耳其-叙利亚三次地震检验之；后半程处理传统生态知识（苏巴克、文化烧荒）与堡垒式保护的对撞，最后进入人类世争论（2024 年地质学界否决建阶）与多物种民族志前沿。</p>\n<p>建议按顺序阅读：生命周期篇提供「阶段是被建构的」这一直觉，生态篇把同一直觉放大到人与环境的关系尺度；两篇在「脆弱性」概念上交汇——老人与儿童在灾害中的差异化处境，正是两个专题共享的分析对象。</p>\n"}